title: Correct public relay auth and room-visibility documentation
---
B111 found that the relay landing page says every route except / and /health requires a Bearer token and describes /list_rooms as public rooms only. Both claims drift from the canonical OCaml implementation.

Acceptance criteria:
- Derive the landing-page auth description from the actual route classes: anonymous read/UI, peer Ed25519, Bearer admin, and handler/self-auth routes.
- State that /list_rooms includes public and gated rooms.
- Explain that /list is not anonymously public, while aliases may still appear through listed-room rosters and public/unlisted history.
- Add a lightweight regression/contract check so the operational copy cannot silently diverge from auth_decision.

Evidence: B111 audit at .collab/research/2026-07-11T02-25-00Z-B111-public-relay-exposure-audit.md.